    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324-a1">

                <pb facs="0776" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg762"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center"><seg type="margin">[8]</seg> *[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turnbull,
                        collector, to Mr. McCulloch, Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office of the Collector of
                            Customs,<lb/>District of Stonington, Connecticut</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stonington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1866-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi>
                        16, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The gun-boat Sciota, recently purchased of
                    the United States Government by parties in New London, has been repairing at
                    Noank, from which place she expects to sail for her destination, Valparaiso. I
                    understand her cargo is to consist of guns, gun-carriages, kerosene oil, oakum,
                    &amp;c. It is the impression here that she is intended for the Chilian navy.</p>
                <pb facs="0777" n="763" xml:id="pg763"/>
                <p>Please inform me if I shall allow her to clear for Valparaiso, or what course I
                    shall pursue in regard to her.</p>
                <p>Yours, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>H. N TURNBULL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh McCulloch</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury, Washington, D.
                                    C.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
